From 5e899ceb5fe0cb7ced1afb65c6aae8b372540d08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 03:44:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Gtk4: TextAlign must move a button's caption

Test1's side buttons are ContentAlignment.BottomCenter and take their icon from a
CSS background at "center 30%", so the caption belongs under the icon. On Gtk4 it
was drawn straight over it.

TextAlign reached SetContentAlignmentCore and stopped there: Button, CheckBox and
RadioButton had all had their override stubbed out during the port with the
comment "Gtk4-removed: self.Xalign". That is true of GtkButton -- Gtk4 deleted
gtk_button_set_alignment along with the rest of GtkMisc -- but GtkLabel kept
xalign and yalign, and they mean exactly what the button's used to; they simply
apply to the space the label itself occupies.

So the caption label carries the alignment now, via a new Gtk4Compat.AlignCaption
next to GetLabelWidget (a Gtk4 check button keeps its caption outside the child
slot, so it has to be found rather than cast to). The label is given Align.Fill
first: sized to its own text it has no slack, and both factors would have nothing
to move within -- every alignment would collapse to centred and the fix would look
applied while changing nothing on screen.

Generic, not keyed to the sample: all nine ContentAlignment values map through,
on all three button types, and a caption-less widget is left alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
